<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-CSFB lifts UBS '97 estimate.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-CSFB lifts UBS '97 estimate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>CS First Boston said on Friday it raised its 1997 earnings per share estimate for Swiss banking group UBS by 23 percent but continued to rate the stock a &quot;hold.&quot;  </p>
<p>CSFB analyst Madeleine Hofmann said the current year would &quot;probably see an outstanding performance in private banking, asset management and investment banking,&quot; and upped its 1997 earnings estimate to 120.1 francs per share.</p>
<p>However, income in these segments was likely to stagnate or even decline in 1998, Hofmann said. She expects earnings per share to drop to 108.2 francs that year.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
